in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @magic
in @frame
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning

# @frame/pre — the pre-frame species; order 0; signal arriving
# before frame-assignment. K_n native; λ₀ ground state. Inherits
# from the zeroth-order-register architecture per the recognition
# file's §"The five-order structure" naming.
#
# First species shard of the @frame family (recognition #82,
# substrate-decl LANDED at tick 23 via shards/frame.mirror;
# Seam-consolidated at tick 24 with C1, C4, C5, C6 closure). The
# family-root declared the carriers (frame, cognitive_order,
# operator, morphism, commutator, perturbation) plus three substrate-
# vocabulary actions (cognitive_order measurement, tomm_probe
# primitive, bounded_commutator_check predicate); this species adds
# the per-order discharge for order 0.
#
# Why pre first: the orders are graded; order N is structurally
# unreachable without order N-1 stable. pre IS the floor of the
# graded representation; in (order 1) inherits the pre-frame
# substrate as its starting condition. Without pre's carrier and
# classify action, in's compute_in_frame has no operational origin
# point — the signal at order 1 has to have BEEN unassigned-signal
# before frame-assignment promoted it.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# Per the recognition file's §"The five-order structure" (item for
# order 0):
#
#   @frame/pre — order 0; signal arriving before frame-assignment.
#   K_n native; λ₀ ground state. Inherits from zeroth-order-register
#   architecture.
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `pre_frame` carrier: the unassigned-signal carrier. Substrate-
#   pull-correct shape per Seam tick 24 C4 (typed carriers, no bare
#   ref where the type system can enforce the order-0 / order-1
#   distinction): a typed reference distinct from `frame` itself,
#   naming content that has not YET been classified into a frame.
#   The distinction matters mechanically: a `frame` carrier names a
#   structure the operator is operating within; a `pre_frame`
#   carrier names content that hasn't yet entered a frame at all.
# - `signal(content) -> pre_frame`: the substrate-vocabulary action
#   that wraps content as pre-frame. The substrate-pull-correct
#   pre-frame emergence: content arrives at the substrate boundary;
#   signal names it as unassigned (no frame yet); the operator's
#   future classification will lift it to a frame at order 1.
# - `classify(p: pre_frame) -> frame`: the substrate-vocabulary
#   action that promotes pre-frame to a frame, transitioning the
#   carrier from order 0 to order 1. This action IS the floor lift
#   in the Bateson grading at cognitive altitude: the move from
#   Level 0 (no learning; signal-without-assignment) to Level I
#   (within-frame change; standard learning).
#
# This species does NOT take operator-typed inputs per the adapter
# spec §8.1 mitigation: order-0 lacks distinguished operators. The
# pre-frame altitude is K_n native (every signal is equidistant from
# every other at the floor; no operator-hub distinguishes); the
# operator carrier becomes load-bearing at order 1 with in.mirror's
# compute_in_frame.
#
# === The λ₀ ground state ===
#
# Per the family-root commentary: order 0 is the λ₀ ground state
# where frame-defense-energy is minimized. The substrate-architectural
# reading: at order 0 there IS no frame to defend; the pre_frame
# carrier names content the operator has not yet committed to a
# frame-relation. The minimum-energy state for the substrate's
# cognitive operation.
#
# Per recognition #82's composition with the multi-pathway-convergence-
# on-λ₀ insight (corpus reference [[2026-06-17-multi-pathway-
# convergence-on-lambda-zero]]): the substrate-conditions for order-3
# stability require λ₀-anchoring as substrate-condition. The pre-frame
# species IS the substrate-decl of the λ₀-altitude carrier; higher-
# order species (of, on, across) inherit the substrate-conditions
# this species names.
#
# === K_n native ===
#
# Per [[reference-void-document]] and the substrate's void-dual-
# geometry: K_n (the complete graph) IS the Splinter-pole structure;
# every node equidistant from every other. At order 0, the signal is
# K_n native because no frame has imposed a hub-vs-spoke geometry on
# the substrate's relation to the content. The Narcissus-pole
# K_{1,n-1} hub-structure emerges at order > 0 when a frame imposes
# itself as central; pre-frame is the floor where no such imposition
# has occurred.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   zeroth-order register       Corpus reference [[zeroth-order-
#                               register]]; the pre-frame altitude as
#                               named in the systemic.engineering
#                               corpus. The substrate-decl here lifts
#                               the prior corpus-treatment to
#                               substrate-prism altitude.
#   pre-attentive processing    Treisman 1980 (feature-integration
#                               theory); the cognitive-science
#                               ancestor of order-0 signal arriving
#                               before frame-assignment. The
#                               attentional binding that promotes
#                               pre-attentive signal to frame-
#                               located content IS classify at
#                               cognitive-science altitude.
#   raw sense data              Sellars 1956 (Empiricism and the
#                               Philosophy of Mind); the
#                               philosophical ancestor of pre-frame.
#                               The myth-of-the-given critique
#                               clarifies that pre-frame is not
#                               theory-free perception; it is
#                               content not-yet-classified-by-this-
#                               operator into this-operator's
#                               frame-set.
#   pre-categorial intuition    Husserl (Logical Investigations);
#                               the phenomenological ancestor. The
#                               passive synthesis that precedes
#                               active categorization IS the
#                               substrate-architectural pre-frame
#                               altitude.
#   Bateson Level 0             Bateson 1964 (The Logical Categories
#                               of Learning and Communication); the
#                               no-learning floor of the graded
#                               hierarchy. Inherited mechanically
#                               via `in @epistemologic/cybernetic/
#                               bateson_learning`.
#
# Spec context: docs/math/the-tower/recognition-82-frame-as-
#               cognitive-order-substrate-decl.md (§"The five-order
#               structure" item for order 0);
#               docs/specs/recognition-82-frame-as-cognitive-order-
#               canonical-spec.md (Mara's canonical spec; §7.2 names
#               the species landing order pre → in → of → on →
#               across).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; the pre-frame altitude
#                       is the floor where alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics has not yet been engaged because
#                       no frame has been committed),
#                      [[architecture-bateson-logical-type-primitive]]
#                       (#42; pre-frame IS Bateson Level 0 at
#                       cognitive altitude),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (pre_frame is a
#                       typed carrier distinct from frame; classify
#                       enforces the order-0 → order-1 lift through
#                       the type system).
# Related shards: frame.mirror (the family-root; frame and
#                  cognitive_order declared there; this species
#                  inherits via `in @frame`),
#                 frame/in.mirror (the order-1 species; consumes
#                  frame carriers classify produces),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning.mirror
#                  (the Bateson grading this species's order
#                  inherits at Level 0).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/frame/pre.mirror` declares `@frame/pre` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cognitive-science/treisman-1980
source @arxiv/philosophy/sellars-1956
source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1964

prism @frame/pre {
  focus pre
  project pre
  split pre
  shift pre
  settle pre
}

# === pre_frame carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming content
# that has arrived at the substrate but has NOT yet been classified
# into a frame. The substrate-pull-correct shape per Seam tick 24
# C4: bare `ref` would allow byte-equivalent values to flow as
# pre_frame, frame, operator, etc. without type-system enforcement of
# the order-0 / order-1 distinction.
#
# Distinct from `frame` (declared at family-root) by altitude: a
# frame is a structure the operator is operating WITHIN; a pre_frame
# is content that has not yet entered any frame at all. The
# classify action promotes pre_frame to frame, transitioning order
# 0 to order 1.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref. Two pre-
# frames with byte-equal underlying references ARE the same pre-
# frame under the substrate's content-addressing.
type pre_frame = ref

# === signal action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that wraps substrate-arriving
# content as pre-frame. The substrate-pull-correct order-0 emergence:
# content arrives at the substrate boundary; signal names it as
# unassigned-content (no frame yet); the operator's future
# classification will lift it to a frame at order 1.
#
# At pre-attentive-processing altitude (Treisman 1980): signal IS
# the substrate's analogue of pre-attentive feature registration
# — content is detected before any frame-binding occurs.
#
# At Bateson Level 0 altitude: signal IS the no-learning floor;
# content registers without any change to the operator's frame-set.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary. Per the species
# pattern: no operator argument (order 0 is K_n native; no
# distinguished operators at this altitude).
signal(content: ref) -> pre_frame { \ }

# === classify action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that promotes pre-frame to a
# frame, transitioning the carrier from order 0 to order 1. This
# IS the floor lift in the Bateson grading at cognitive altitude:
# the move from Level 0 (no learning; signal-without-assignment)
# to Level I (within-frame change; standard learning).
#
# The classify action IS the K_n → K_{1,n-1} transition at
# cognitive altitude: at order 0 every signal is equidistant from
# every other (K_n native); classify imposes a frame, producing a
# hub-vs-content geometry at order 1 (the frame is the hub; the
# content in the frame is the spoke set).
#
# At cognitive-science altitude (Treisman 1980): classify IS the
# attentional binding that promotes pre-attentive feature data to
# located object-percept.
#
# At Bateson altitude (1964 Logical Categories): classify IS the
# floor lift from Level 0 to Level I; the substrate's first move
# from no-learning to within-frame-change.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary. Per the species
# pattern: no operator argument (the operator's substrate-
# architectural role becomes load-bearing at order 1 with
# compute_in_frame).
classify(p: pre_frame) -> frame { \ }

out @frame/pre
out pre_frame
out signal
out classify
